  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Cities 2 W1 - Tbilisi Metro Modernisation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A sovereign loan of up to EUR 50.6 million to Georgia (tranched) to be on-lent  to the city of Tbilisi (the &quot;City&quot;) for the benefit of Tbilisi Transport  Company Ltd (the &quot;Company&quot;), a municipal company operating buses, the metro  system and cable cars in Tbilisi.  The investment will improve the reliability, safety and efficiency of public  transport through the upgrade and rehabilitation of 12 metro stations (the  &quot;Project&quot;).     The Project is part of a broader programme aiming to assist the City in  reforming its management of public transport by financing the renewal of bus  and metro systems, and network restructuring.</narrative>
  </description>
